# Credentials — public repository, never commit
.ps/session
.ps/cookies*

# Cache (regenerable, large)
.ps/catalog.json

# The tracker's exclusive lock on this repository. It normally lives inside .git/, where git
# cannot see it; this covers the one case where it cannot — a run from before `git init`.
.programmers-tracker.lock

# OS
.DS_Store

# The tracker's working state, added by the server itself. It lives here so that it sits
# beside the records it describes, and it is not records: frames still being captured,
# per-problem timers, when the last push succeeded. `.ps/raw/recorded/` keeps one file
# per code run, and a run gets pressed dozens of times while solving one problem —
# committing them would bury your solving history in its own scratch work.
.ps/


# The other editor's state, here for the same reason as the line above (#304). This is a
# Kotlin project, so a vault opened in IntelliJ is not an edge case — and `git add --all`
# cannot tell a window layout from a record any better than it could tell a graph zoom.
# Delete this line if you would rather version it; nothing else depends on it.
.idea/

# Obsidian's window layout — which panes are open, where they are scrolled. It changes
# because the vault was *opened*, and `git add --all` cannot tell that from a record: one
# backup commit carried nothing else, under a message about records (#234).
#
# Only this file. `graph.json` beside it holds the colour groups you built, and the rest
# are settings — versioning them is why a vault cloned onto another machine opens
# configured rather than blank, which is the same promise the records themselves make
# (#306, narrowing the rule that took the whole directory).
.obsidian/workspace.json

# The same file, from the phone.
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# The rest of that editor's state, which the line above cannot reach: IntelliJ writes
# <project>.iml at the ROOT, not inside .idea/. It lists every problem directory it has
# indexed, so it outlives the records it names — measured on a repository whose history
# had been cleared, still publishing four problem titles, two of them already deleted
# (#323). Same escape hatch as the line above.
*.iml
